sig_catch: define SA_RESTART to 0 where the system lacks it

QNX does not implement SA_RESTART (its <signal.h> has it commented out
as "not supported yet"). Without it an interrupted system call returns
EINTR, which skalibs' I/O primitives already retry on (the safe wrappers
loop on EINTR), so 0 is the honest value.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/libstddjb/sig_catch.c
+++ b/src/libstddjb/sig_catch.c
@@ -11,6 +11,11 @@
 #include <skalibs/sig.h>
 #include <skalibs/nsig.h>
 
+#ifndef SA_RESTART
+  /* QNX: not implemented (commented out in <signal.h>) */
+# define SA_RESTART 0
+#endif
+
  /*
    We don't want to fail on non-catchable signals,
    even if sigaction() does.
